      "exampleTransliteration": "urīdu an adhhaba ilā l-bayti",
      "exampleEnglish": "I want to go home.",
      "grammarNote": "'I want to [verb]' is simply أُرِيدُ (level 15) + أَنْ (level 48) + a present-tense verb — the exact same combination that made يَسْتَطِيعُ أَنْ ('can', level 48) work. No new vocabulary is needed at all; this is a pure grammar combination showing how far your existing pieces stretch. لِأَنَّ ('because') is this level's one genuinely new word, useful for explaining WHY you want something: أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَذْهَبَ لِأَنِّي جَائِعٌ ('I want to go because I'm hungry').",
